WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.327
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:09.199
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:17.922
Unit nine: Part 4: Tours, Meetings and Speeches. Today you will follow longer talks, understand structure and use graphics.

4
00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:20.839
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.033
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.583
Tour.

7
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.211
Tour means a guided visit.

8
00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:31.305
The tour starts at ten.

9
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:34.047
Your turn. Say: Tour.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.634
Tour.

11
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.559
Presentation.

12
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.026
Presentation means a talk with slides.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:45.930
The presentation lasts twenty minutes.

14
00:00:46.517 --> 00:00:49.854
Your turn. Say: Presentation.

15
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.864
Presentation.

16
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:55.455
Quarter.

17
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.879
Quarter means three months of a business year.

18
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:01.576
Sales rose in the third quarter.

19
00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:04.441
Your turn. Say: Quarter.

20
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.139
Quarter.

21
00:01:08.883 --> 00:01:09.699
Revenue.

22
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:13.275
Revenue means money a company earns.

23
00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:15.883
Revenue increased by ten percent.

24
00:01:16.483 --> 00:01:18.683
Your turn. Say: Revenue.

25
00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:22.349
Revenue.

26
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:23.992
Welcome.

27
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:26.878
Welcome means to greet someone.

28
00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:29.309
I'd like to welcome our guests.

29
00:01:29.917 --> 00:01:32.070
Your turn. Say: Welcome.

30
00:01:34.933 --> 00:01:35.853
Welcome.

31
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:37.641
Facility.

32
00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:42.078
Facility means a building or area used for a purpose.

33
00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:44.311
The facility has a gym.

34
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:47.569
Your turn. Say: Facility.

35
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:51.609
Facility.

36
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.351
Retire.

37
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.127
Retire means to stop working after a career.

38
00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.774
Mr. Lee will retire next month.

39
00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:03.593
Your turn. Say: Retire.

40
00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:07.481
Retire.

41
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:09.136
Applaud.

42
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.382
Applaud means to clap to show thanks.

43
00:02:12.983 --> 00:02:14.693
Let's applaud our speaker.

44
00:02:15.283 --> 00:02:17.912
Your turn. Say: Applaud.

45
00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:21.652
Applaud.

46
00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:26.083
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:29.868
Visal, what types of talks appear in Part 4?

48
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:42.538
Common talks include a guide welcoming a tour group, a manager giving a meeting report, a speech at an event and a radio news item.

49
00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.951
What is the structure of a business speech?

50
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:57.620
A speaker welcomes people, states the topic, gives the main points and then thanks the listeners. Signposts like first, next and finally help you follow.

51
00:02:58.717 --> 00:03:01.390
How do I answer graphic questions in Part 4?

52
00:03:02.483 --> 00:03:13.750
Study the chart first. If the speaker says the highest revenue was in the third quarter, find that quarter in the graphic and choose the matching label or number.

53
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.261
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.117 --> 00:03:21.578
Grammar focus: Strategy: follow the structure of the talk.

55
00:03:21.878 --> 00:03:23.099
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.783 --> 00:03:26.851
Revenue increased by ten percent in the third quarter.

57
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.690
First, I'll welcome you; next, I'll explain the schedule.

58
00:03:31.633 --> 00:03:38.532
Follow signposts, match the speaker's numbers with the graphic, and listen to the last lines for thanks and the next step.

59
00:03:39.283 --> 00:03:42.737
Be careful! Don't say: I ignore the signposts.

60
00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.804
Say: I follow the signposts.

61
00:03:47.104 --> 00:03:48.883
Signposts show order.

62
00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:52.156
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:52.967 --> 00:03:54.293
A Quarterly Meeting.

64
00:03:54.593 --> 00:03:57.417
A manager welcomes staff to the quarterly meeting.

65
00:03:58.433 --> 00:04:01.826
She says revenue increased by ten percent in the third quarter.

66
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:05.297
She shows a chart with sales in four regions.

67
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.659
The northern region had the highest figure.

68
00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:12.537
She thanks everyone and introduces the next speaker.

69
00:04:13.633 --> 00:04:17.554
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:18.417 --> 00:04:19.778
A quarter is blank.

71
00:04:20.078 --> 00:04:23.940
A, three months. B, one week. C, one year.

72
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.546
The answer is A: three months.

73
00:04:30.683 --> 00:04:32.532
Revenue increased by blank.

74
00:04:32.832 --> 00:04:36.787
A, one percent. B, ten percent. C, five percent.

75
00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:42.762
The answer is B: ten percent.

76
00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:46.009
Which region had the highest figure?

77
00:04:46.309 --> 00:04:50.473
A, the south. B, the east. C, the northern region.

78
00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.462
The answer is C: the northern region.

79
00:04:57.617 --> 00:05:00.348
Signposts like first and next show blank.

80
00:05:00.648 --> 00:05:04.289
A, structure. B, spelling. C, a map.

81
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:09.612
The answer is A: structure.

82
00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.680
What does the manager do at the end?

83
00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:17.121
A, leave. B, thank everyone. C, cancel the meeting.

84
00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:23.061
The answer is B: thank everyone.

85
00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:27.256
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:28.117 --> 00:05:30.732
How do you follow a longer talk in Part 4?

87
00:05:39.517 --> 00:05:40.878
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:41.178 --> 00:05:55.303
I listen for the welcome and the topic, then follow signposts such as first, next and finally. I match numbers with the graphic if there is one. In the last lines I listen for thanks and the next step.

89
00:05:55.603 --> 00:05:57.464
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:03.847
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: follow the structure of the talk.

91
00:06:04.147 --> 00:06:08.784
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:09.084 --> 00:06:11.690
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

93
00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:15.293
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

